{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And she weaned</b> — The tribes that went into exile bore children in their exile, and there they remained and did not return to their land; therefore he called them Lo-Ammi." "<b>And I will not be</b> — to them as Elohim, and out of the abundance of wrath he did not mention it [i.e., the divine name]."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The lemma ותגמל (\"and she weaned\") is applied to the tribes metaphorically; Ibn Ezra reads the nursing/weaning as the raising of children born in exile.", 1 "The pronoun suffix in לא הזכירו could target the name Elohim or the people; translated literally to preserve the ambiguity."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:43.462345450Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}